@startuml
' UC17.1 - Thêm học liệu Video
autonumber "<b>0.</b> "
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor white
skinparam BoundaryBackgroundColor white
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor black
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam MaxMessageSize 200

' AS-IS evidence; paths are relative to the workspace root.
' UC/BR: docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_UseCase.docx (UC17.1) and
' docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_QuyTacNghiepVu.docx (BR-151, BR-286, BR-288, BR-285, BR-51).
' Both have core revision 1; no business release identifier was found.
' The requested docs/ documents are under docs/uml/docs/; docs/source-of-truth is absent.
' UI: frontend/src/pages/instructor/course.builder.material.video.add.tsx:89;
' context query :106, handleFile :131, handleSave :169, error reload :229.
' Route: frontend/src/router.tsx:457, :459 and :497 (Instructor-protected Builder child).
' Wrappers: frontend/src/services/course.service.ts:145 and :155.
' Transport: frontend/src/services/axios.customize.ts:47, :61 and :64;
' URL selection: frontend/src/config/env.ts:13; frontend/.env.development:10 = localhost:8080.
' No frontend .env/.env.local/.env.development.local or process URL overrides found.
' Gateway: gateway/api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:2, :40 (courses predicate :43).
' Course bootstrap: services/course-service/src/main.ts:40 (api prefix, URI v1).
' Controller: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.controller.ts:184 and :194.
' Service: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.service.ts:986 and :1091.
' Repository: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.repository.ts:871, :882, :922, :937.
' DTO: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/dto/create-video-material.dto.ts:10.
' Multipart cap: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/course-values.ts:31 (500 MiB).
' Tenant adapter: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/clients/tenant/tenant.client.ts:64.
' Adapter wiring: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.module.ts:14 (5000 ms, no redirects).
' Direct Tenant URL: services/course-service/.env:4 = http://localhost:8084.
' Tenant controller: services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.controller.ts:22;
' service : services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.service.ts:128;
' repository: services/tenant-service/src/modules/subscriptions/subscriptions.repository.ts:20.
' Tenant prefix/version: services/tenant-service/src/main.ts:34.
' Storage wiring: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/storage/storage.module.ts:7;
' provider selection: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/storage/storage.provider.ts:31.
' All three Cloudinary configuration values are present locally; values are not disclosed.
' Provider: libraries/ts-storage/src/providers/cloudinary/cloudinary.provider.ts:31 (upload),
' :61 (delete), :102 (uploadBuffer), :187 (mapUploadResult).
' Storage validation: libraries/ts-storage/src/validators/file.validator.ts:7.
' Models: services/course-service/prisma/schema.prisma:10, :104, :126, :187;
' services/tenant-service/prisma/schema.prisma:133 (Subscription).
' PrismaService in each service uses its own DATABASE_URL; verified DB names appear below.
' Local development configuration is represented; running servers and Cloudinary access are unverified.

actor Instructor
boundary "Add Video Material Page" as Screen
participant ":ApiGateway" as Gateway
participant ":CoursesController" as Controller
participant ":CoursesService" as Service
participant ":CoursesRepository" as Repository
participant ":SubscriptionsController" as SubscriptionsController
participant ":SubscriptionsService" as SubscriptionsService
participant ":SubscriptionsRepository" as SubscriptionsRepository
participant ":CloudinaryStorageProvider" as Storage
participant "Cloudinary" as Cloudinary
database "course_db" as CourseDB
database "tenant_db" as TenantDB

' Preconditions: authenticated Instructor and already loaded Course Builder shell.
' Shared structure/Assessment-outline preparation is excluded from this upload operation.
' TenantClient is hidden: the Service calls the receiving controller directly using
' the actual REST endpoint, internal key and trusted user/organization/role headers.
' Ordinary JWT middleware and token refresh are omitted.
activate Instructor
Instructor -> Screen: Open Add Video Material
activate Screen
Screen -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/video-upload-context
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Controller: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/video-upload-context
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: getVideoUploadContext(user, courseId, lessonId)
activate Service

' Outcome-level context trace: successful preparation expands its actual reads.
' Failed attempts do not imply successful DB work or a reply after a timeout.
alt Upload context loaded successfully
  ' Role=INSTRUCTOR and organizationId are checked before this read.
  Service -> Repository: findLessonForMaterialUpload\nCurrent organization and instructor
  activate Repository
  Repository -> CourseDB: Read assigned Lesson and Course state
  activate CourseDB
  CourseDB -->> Repository: Scoped Lesson and Course
  deactivate CourseDB
  Repository -->> Service: Scoped Lesson and Course
  deactivate Repository

  par Read platform limits
    Service -> Repository: getVideoSettings()
    activate Repository
    Repository -> CourseDB: Read latest local PlatformSetting
    activate CourseDB
    CourseDB -->> Repository: Video limits and MIME types
    deactivate CourseDB
    Repository -->> Service: Video settings
    deactivate Repository
  and Read Subscription policy
    Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
    activate SubscriptionsController
    SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
    activate SubscriptionsService
    SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
    activate SubscriptionsRepository
    SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
    activate TenantDB
    TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
    deactivate TenantDB
    SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
    deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
    ' Only Active with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits uploads; others return canUpload=false.
    SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission, status and storage limit
    deactivate SubscriptionsService
    SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
    deactivate SubscriptionsController
  and Read organization usage
    Service -> Repository: getOrganizationStoredBytes(organizationId)
    activate Repository
    Repository -> CourseDB: Sum Ready, unreleased MediaFile bytes
    activate CourseDB
    CourseDB -->> Repository: Used bytes
    deactivate CourseDB
    Repository -->> Service: Used bytes
    deactivate Repository
  end
  Service -->> Controller: Upload eligibility, limits and remaining bytes
  deactivate Service
  Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK - upload context
  deactivate Controller
  Gateway -->> Screen: Upload context
  deactivate Gateway

  alt Upload eligibility checked successfully\nUpload allowed
    Screen -->> Instructor: Show upload form and limits\nLocked Course permits Optional only
    Instructor -> Screen: Choose Video, title and requirement
    Screen -> Screen: Validate file and fields
    activate Screen
    deactivate Screen

    alt Form validated successfully
      Instructor -> Screen: Click Upload Video
      ' FormData has title, string isRequired and binary file. Locked context forces false.
      ' Axios POST timeout=15 minutes; progress reports browser-to-backend bytes only.
      Screen -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/videos\nMultipart: title, isRequired, file
      activate Gateway
      Gateway -> Controller: POST /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/videos\nMultipart file and trusted user context
      activate Controller
      ' FileInterceptor buffers one file in memory; files=1, fields=2, parts=3, max=500 MiB.
      ' Multipart/DTO rejection can stop before the Service; those framework traces are omitted.
      Controller -> Service: uploadVideoMaterial(user, courseId, lessonId, dto, file)
      activate Service

      ' Outcome-level upload trace: only success expands all accepted checks and writes.
      ' The failed operand groups early rejection, remote failures and failed finalization.
      alt Video created successfully
        Service -> Repository: Recheck assigned Lesson and load Video settings
        activate Repository
        ' Two actual sequential methods: findLessonForMaterialUpload then getVideoSettings.
        Repository -> CourseDB: Read current Lesson state and Video limits
        activate CourseDB
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Scoped Lesson and settings
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: Scoped Lesson and settings
        deactivate Repository
        Service -> Service: Validate Course state, size and Video signature
        activate Service
        ' Reject Submitted/disabled Course or Lesson; Locked+isRequired=true ->409.
        ' Effective byte limit=min(PlatformSetting.maxVideoSizeBytes, 500 MiB).
        ' Signature: ftyp at byte 4 for mp4/mov; EBML magic for webm; MIME must be allowed.
        deactivate Service
        Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
        activate SubscriptionsController
        SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
        activate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
        activate SubscriptionsRepository
        SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
        activate TenantDB
        TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
        deactivate TenantDB
        SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
        deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
        ' Only Active with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits uploads; others return canUpload=false.
        SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission, status and storage limit
        deactivate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
        deactivate SubscriptionsController
        ' Policy must allow upload; then compare incoming size against remaining quota.
        Service -> Repository: Check organization storage usage
        activate Repository
        Repository -> CourseDB: Sum Ready, unreleased MediaFile bytes
        activate CourseDB
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Used bytes
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: Used bytes
        deactivate Repository

        Service -> Storage: Upload Video buffer
        activate Storage
        Storage -> Cloudinary: Upload Video in 20 MiB chunks
        activate Cloudinary
        Cloudinary -->> Storage: Final stored-file metadata
        deactivate Cloudinary
        Storage -->> Service: Stored file and duration
        deactivate Storage
        Service -> Service: Validate returned format, duration and size
        activate Service
        ' Require video resourceType, matching mp4/webm/mov format, positive integer duration,
        ' duration <= maxVideoDurationMinutes*60, and positive size within effective byte limit.
        ' Provider rounds Cloudinary duration up to whole seconds before this check.
        deactivate Service
        ' A fresh policy is requested after upload, before the database transaction.
        Service -> SubscriptionsController: GET /api/v1/subscriptions/internal/instructor-material-upload-policy
        activate SubscriptionsController
        SubscriptionsController -> SubscriptionsService: getInstructorMaterialUploadPolicy(user)
        activate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsService -> SubscriptionsRepository: findCurrent(organizationId)
        activate SubscriptionsRepository
        SubscriptionsRepository -> TenantDB: Read current organization Subscription
        activate TenantDB
        TenantDB -->> SubscriptionsRepository: Subscription or none
        deactivate TenantDB
        SubscriptionsRepository -->> SubscriptionsService: Subscription or none
        deactivate SubscriptionsRepository
        ' Only Active with startsAt <= now < expiresAt permits uploads; others return canUpload=false.
        SubscriptionsService -->> SubscriptionsController: Permission, status and storage limit
        deactivate SubscriptionsService
        SubscriptionsController -->> Service: 200 OK - upload policy
        deactivate SubscriptionsController
        Service -> Repository: createVideoMaterialWithQuota(...)
        activate Repository
        Repository -> CourseDB: Recheck quota and Course under locks\nSave MediaFile and append Video material
        activate CourseDB
        ' One transaction, timeout=20 seconds: upsert/lock organization_quota_locks,
        ' lock Course row, recheck tenant/chain owner/Submitted/disabled/Locked-required,
        ' recompute used bytes with the latest policy limit, then insert both records.
        ' MediaFile: purpose=LessonVideo, status=Ready, durationSeconds and storage metadata.
        ' Material: materialType=Video, isRequired=dto.isRequired, fileId=new MediaFile.id.
        ' position=max existing Lesson position+1, including for unlocked Courses.
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Committed Video material
        deactivate CourseDB
        Repository -->> Service: CREATED and material
        deactivate Repository
        Service -->> Controller: Material, file size and duration
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 201 Created - Video material
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Created material ID
        deactivate Gateway
        Screen -->> Instructor: Show success and open material list
      else Video creation failed
        activate Gateway
        activate Controller
        activate Service
        ' 400: missing/empty file or title, disallowed MIME/signature, bad metadata/duration.
        ' 413: multipart/technical size cap; 403: wrong role or disallowed Subscription.
        ' 404: missing Lesson, mismatched Course/tenant/owner.
        ' 409: Submitted, disabled, Locked-required or quota insufficient.
        ' Policy non-2xx/malformed response/transport error/5000 ms timeout ->503;
        ' no automatic policy retry or permissive fallback; no reply after timeout assumed.
        ' StorageProviderError ->503; storage validation ->400; unexpected DB error ->500.
        ' Successful remote upload/DB insertion is not assumed in this failed operand.
        opt Stored file returned and transaction not committed
          Service -> Storage: Delete uncommitted uploaded file
          activate Storage
          Storage -> Cloudinary: Delete stored resource
          activate Cloudinary
          Cloudinary -->> Storage: Deletion result or error
          deactivate Cloudinary
          Storage -->> Service: Cleanup result or error
          deactivate Storage
          ' Finally block awaits best-effort cleanup and preserves the original failure.
        end
        Service -->> Controller: Validation, policy, upload or persistence error
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 400 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 413 / 503 or 500
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Video creation error
        deactivate Gateway
        Screen -->> Instructor: Show upload error
        ' handleSave.catch calls query.reload() for every failed attempt.
        Screen -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/video-upload-context
        activate Gateway
        Gateway -> Controller: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/materials/video-upload-context
        activate Controller
        Controller -> Service: Reload upload context
        activate Service
        ' Same getVideoUploadContext method as expanded above, including its Tenant REST
        ' and parallel scoped settings/usage reads. Repeated internals are not expanded.
        ' The result can be refreshed/blocked context, or a load error; no success assumed.
        Service -->> Controller: Refreshed context or load error
        deactivate Service
        Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK or context error
        deactivate Controller
        Gateway -->> Screen: Context result
        deactivate Gateway
        Screen -->> Instructor: Show refreshed form, block reason or load error
      end
    else Form validation failed
      ' No POST: invalid title, missing/empty file, disallowed MIME, excessive size or quota.
      Screen -->> Instructor: Show validation error
    end
  else Upload eligibility failed
    ' Context GET succeeds with canUpload=false for Submitted/disabled Course or Lesson,
    ' or a Subscription outside Active and its validity period. Locked alone is allowed.
    ' Zero remaining quota is shown in context; per-file validation then blocks positive files.
    Screen -->> Instructor: Show block reason and disable upload
  end
else Upload context loading failed
  activate Gateway
  activate Controller
  activate Service
  ' Wrong role/missing organization ->403, inaccessible Lesson ->404;
  ' absent PlatformSetting or Tenant verification failure ->503; DB/transport errors grouped.
  ' Initial context failure emits no multipart POST and no storage upload.
  Service -->> Controller: Context access or verification error
  deactivate Service
  Controller -->> Gateway: 403 / 404 / 503 or server error
  deactivate Controller
  Gateway -->> Screen: Context load error
  deactivate Gateway
  Screen -->> Instructor: Show load error and Try again
end
deactivate Screen
deactivate Instructor

' BR-151/285/286: upload checks platform limits and quota, blocks Submitted/disabled,
' and accepts only Optional on Locked Courses. Final transaction repeats mutable checks.
' Lesson/Module/Course organizationId and Course.chain.instructorId scope access.
' BR-288 usage aggregates Ready, unreleased MediaFile rows once, without joining
' Material/version references. There is no explicit purpose whitelist in that aggregate;
' the organization-wide quota lock serializes this transaction's quota check and creation.
' BR-51: persist provider-derived durationSeconds and isRequired; this upload does not
' open Course detail, recalculate estimated duration or publish a duration-change event.
' MIME default in schema is video/mp4; actual allowed types come from the latest local
' PlatformSetting row, intersected implicitly with the implemented mp4/webm/quicktime checks.
' No live DB rows were read, so actual configured numeric limits are not claimed.
' Quota/Subscription check is not one cross-database transaction: latest Tenant policy
' may change after being read. Quota locking covers cooperating Course DB writers only.
' Cleanup failure is logged, not retried; if provider upload throws before storedFile
' is assigned, this service has no returned storage key for cleanup of remote remnants.
' Browser timeout/network loss does not prove backend cancellation or transaction rollback.
' UI error caveat: axios.customize.ts resolves HTTP error bodies. Missing response.data.id
' throws a plain Error, so getUploadErrorMessage may display generic Network error rather
' than the intended status-specific message. query.reload() still runs.
' Browser progress reaching 100% does not mean Cloudinary/DB work has finished.
' Success navigates to UC17; loading that list is outside this creation diagram.
' No direct browser-to-Cloudinary/MinIO, presigned URL, LearningClient, Kafka, notification,
' audit, Reading upload, replacement or user-triggered material deletion is executed here.
@enduml
